{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4041748","formula":"C₂₆H₂₇NO","hill":"C26H27NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":26.0,"H":27.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"JWH-210","ru":"JWH-210"},"descriptions":{"en":"JWH-210 is an analgesic chemical from the naphthoylindole family, which acts as a potent cannabinoid agonist at both the CB1 and CB2 receptors, with Ki values of 0.46 nM at CB1 and 0.69 nM at CB2. It is one of the most potent 4-substituted naphthoyl derivatives in the naphthoylindole series, having a higher binding affinity (i.e. lower Ki) at CB1 than both its 4-methyl and 4-n-propyl homologues JWH-122 (CB1 Ki 0.69 nM) and JWH-182 (CB1 Ki 0.65 nM) respectively, and than the 4-methoxy compound JWH-081 (CB1 Ki 1.2 nM).","ru":"JWH-210 — органическое химическое соединение. Является анальгетиком, принадлежащим к семейству нафтоилиндолов."},"fame":7,"pubchemCid":45270396,"mass":369.5,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCN1C=C(C2=CC=CC=C21)C(=O)C3=CC=C(C4=CC=CC=C43)CC","inchikey":"LACIUQLUNACUKC-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"(4-ethylnaphthalen-1-yl)-(1-pentylindol-3-yl)methanone","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"45270396","atoms":55,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":0.035,"y":-2.737,"z":1.253,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.374,"y":0.207,"z":-1.238,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.785,"y":1.261,"z":-2.141,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.22,"y":-0.602,"z":-0.514,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.198,"y":2.557,"z":-1.433,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.42,"y":-1.477,"z":0.224,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.066,"y":-1.164,"z":-0.083,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.07,"y":-0.125,"z":-0.984,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.105,"y":3.113,"z":-0.515,"el":"C"},{"x":0.17,"y":-1.81,"z":0.446,"el":"C"},{"x":1.506,"y":-1.381,"z":0.041,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.591,"y":4.354,"z":0.234,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.618,"y":-0.626,"z":-0.457,"el":"C"},{"x":2.218,"y":-0.384,"z":0.727,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.043,"y":